# Optional environment for the Orca server unit on Linux (--role server), written as Environment= lines.
# Nothing is set by default. Set values in manifest/local/orca-serve.env (git-ignored), one KEY=VALUE per line;
# a key there replaces the same key here. Only these keys are accepted:
#   ORCA_TERMINAL_PROCESS_CEILING=<n>      64 or more: processes per terminal (experimental upstream)
#   ORCA_TERMINAL_MEMORY_MAX=<size>        256M or more: memory per terminal; sizes take K, M, G or T
#   ORCA_TERMINAL_MEMORY_SWAP_MAX=<size>   swap per terminal; 0 means no swap
# The limits need systemd with cgroup v2 and linger (which --apply --role server turns on). Orca reads them when its
# terminal host starts, and that process outlives a restart of the unit, so new limits apply after a reboot.
